                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Hospitals are legally required to treat anyone in an emergency, even if they can\u2019t pay. Cutting Medicaid just means hospitals absorb the cost, instead of being reimbursed. \n\nIn addition, if patients can\u2019t get regular, preventative care, they resort to emergency rooms. This means emergency rooms will be overwhelmed.",
